            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0209" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1926v01/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15/219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-04-17T12:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 17,
                                1926—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 17—11:04
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>33. Your 93, April 12, via Paris. Belgian Foreign Office indicates a disposition
                    not to adopt any procedure which would cause American <pb facs="0210" n="78"
                        xml:id="pg78"/> Government difficulties at forthcoming meeting of the
                    Preparatory Commission in Geneva. Belgian Government does not desire
                    postponement of meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
